WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.410
Believe it or not, the stars we know and love
as Marvel's mightiest heroes weren't always

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.899
the studio's first choice.

00:00:05.899 --> 00:00:10.460
Assembling the right cast for the Marvel Cinematic
Universe was a Nick Fury-sized task that took

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:14.280
years, and still Marvel couldn't get their
top picks all of the time.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.010
Here are some actors who were almost cast
as an Avenger.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.050
Sam Rockwell as Iron Man

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:23.270
Iron Man director Jon Favreau has publicly
acknowledged that the quirky character actor

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:26.250
was someone he seriously considered for Tony
Stark.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.610
Favreau told Hero Complex,

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:30.110
"He was one of the actors I was looking at
for Tony Stark.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:33.270
Of course, when I met with Robert [Downey
Jr.] there was nobody else on my mind."

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:38.030
Favreau liked Rockwell so much that he cast
him in Iron Man 2 as Justin Hammer, a guy

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:40.300
who really, really wishes he was Tony Stark.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:43.430
"This Iron Man doll, it's my nephew Timmy's.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:46.960
Timmy looks up to you, he wants to be you.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.440
Don't disappoint him."

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.520
Timothy Olyphant as Iron Man

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:55.420
Olyphant has headlined both Deadwood and Justified,
two beloved, critically acclaimed TV series.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:58.050
But he was looking to take his film career
up a notch.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:01.670
His management team was able to get him onto
Jon Favreau's short list for Iron Man.

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:05.819
His auditions went well, and he even filmed
a screen test, but due to poor timing, it

00:01:05.819 --> 00:01:07.439
didn't work out in his favor.

00:01:07.439 --> 00:01:12.710
"Wonderful actor, Robert Downey Jr. and I,
we screen tested on the same day.

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:15.369
And I'm still waiting to hear back."

00:01:15.369 --> 00:01:18.459
Eliza Dushku as Black Widow

00:01:18.459 --> 00:01:23.249
Best known for her roles on cult TV shows
like Joss Whedon's Buffy the Vampire Slayer

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:27.740
and Dollhouse, Dushku publicly campaigned
for the role of Black Widow in Iron Man 2.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:31.499
She appeared on The Howard Stern Show to specify
exactly why she wanted the role.

00:01:31.499 --> 00:01:34.100
"I just watched Iron Man recently.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.459
Robert Downey Jr.'s so hot.

00:01:35.459 --> 00:01:39.869
And they're doing Iron Man 2, and I am so
perfect for the Black Widow character.

00:01:39.869 --> 00:01:42.600
I just need to get into it, they need to understand."

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:46.310
She also added that she'd learned a lot of
Russian for an episode of Dollhouse, which

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:48.619
would come in handy playing the Russian character.

00:01:48.619 --> 00:01:52.520
Even though she was a Joss Whedon favorite,
the role went to Scarlett Johansson.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.130
Emily Blunt as Black Widow

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:58.299
The British star of The Devil Wears Prada
was also one of Marvel's top choices to play

00:01:58.299 --> 00:02:00.520
Black Widow in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:05.530
The studio was reportedly very close to signing
her, until everyone realized a scheduling

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:10.789
conflict couldn't be overcome: her starring
role in the 2010 adaptation of Gulliver's

00:02:10.789 --> 00:02:14.380
Travels with Jack Black, which was a critical
disaster.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:16.120
John Krasinski as Captain America

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:20.819
Coincidentally, Emily Blunt's husband, John
Krasinski of The Office, was very close to

00:02:20.819 --> 00:02:25.540
portraying squeaky-clean, all-American good
guy Steve Rogers and his alter ego, Captain

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:26.540
America.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:30.939
In 2010, news outlets reported that he was
very close to signing on the dotted line,

00:02:30.939 --> 00:02:34.709
but that wasn't quite true, as Krasinski relayed
on Conan in 2016.

00:02:34.709 --> 00:02:38.530
"I was putting on the suit just watching it,
I was like 'This is so amazing' and I got

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:42.290
about right to my waist, I was still shirtless,
feeling pretty good about myself, it wasn't

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:44.590
13 hours yet, but I felt pretty good.

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:48.110
And all the sudden Chris Hemsworth walked
by as Thor and he's like 'Hey mate.'

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:49.550
And I went 'I'm good.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:50.690
This is stupid.'"

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:52.909
Still, it seems like he settled for the next
best thing.

00:02:52.909 --> 00:02:55.500
"Look everyone it's not Spider-Man, it's John
Krasinski.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:56.500
Alright?

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:57.689
Great, now let's go inside."

00:02:57.689 --> 00:02:59.519
"Can't believe you did that."

00:02:59.519 --> 00:03:01.510
David Duchovny as The Hulk

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:05.540
Over the past decade or so, three different
actors have played the iconic angry green

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:06.540
guy.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:11.630
Eric Bana landed the role in Ang Lee's brainy
2003 Hulk, but opted not to return for a sequel,

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:14.549
possibly because there were rumors it would
be released direct-to-video.

00:03:14.549 --> 00:03:19.099
When Marvel decided to reboot the Hulk, David
Duchovny reportedly had the part locked up,

00:03:19.099 --> 00:03:22.819
according to an AOL interview with Marvel's
then-vice chairman Peter Cuneo.

00:03:22.819 --> 00:03:26.189
Ultimately, Ed Norton aggressively lobbied
for the part and won.

00:03:26.189 --> 00:03:30.800
Norton left after one Hulk film to avoid being
typecast, according to an interview with NPR.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:35.120
Marvel replaced him with Mark Ruffalo, again
leaving the terminally-chill David Duchovny

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:36.470
out of the equation.

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:37.939
Tom Hiddleston as Thor

00:03:37.939 --> 00:03:42.049
Before Tom Hiddleston brought the villainous
Loki to life, Marvel was interested in him

00:03:42.049 --> 00:03:45.689
for the role of Thor himself, according to
an interview on Chelsea Lately.

00:03:45.689 --> 00:03:50.109
"You auditioned for Thor, the actual Thor
the character, and you didn't get it, you

00:03:50.109 --> 00:03:55.239
built, you worked out you got yourself beefed
up and then you were rejected?"

00:03:55.239 --> 00:03:56.239
"Coldly.

00:03:56.239 --> 00:03:57.239
Blindly."

00:03:57.239 --> 00:04:00.959
After his screen test, filmmakers realized
he was better suited for the role of Loki,

00:04:00.959 --> 00:04:02.099
Thor's manipulative half-brother.

00:04:02.099 --> 00:04:06.359
Fortunately, fans can still check out his
audition tape, which appears as a bonus feature

00:04:06.359 --> 00:04:08.469
on the Thor: The Dark World Blu-ray.

00:04:08.469 --> 00:04:10.540
Alexander Skarsgard as Thor

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:14.810
The Scandinavian star of True Blood definitely
looked the part of the ancient Norse god of

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:15.810
thunder.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:19.510
Alexander Skarsgard made it all the way to
the final round of casting for Thor, even

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:22.750
filming a screen test in costume, complete
with helmet and hammer.

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:27.750
He really wanted the part, but Marvel went
with Australian hunk Chris Hemsworth instead.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.570
Jensen Ackles as Hawkeye

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:33.890
Even Hawkeye, the least famous, least popular,
and least super-powered of all of the Avengers

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:35.580
was the subject of a casting battle.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.280
That was harsh, poor Hawkeye.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:41.350
As it went down, the role of Hawkeye was nearly
offered up as a kind of consolation prize

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:45.520
to Supernatural star Jensen Ackles, who had
auditioned to play Captain America.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:48.980
Marvel executives liked him, though, and invited
him to consider playing Hawkeye.

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:52.690
Ackles passed because he couldn't get out
of his arduous Supernatural shooting schedule,

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:56.240
which is now in its twelfth season and has
recently became the longest-running sci-fi

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:57.460
show in the US.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:58.460
Sorry, Smallville.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:04:59.660
Thanks for watching!

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:03.180
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:06.720
And leave us a comment to let us know who
you think should've been considered for Avengers

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:07.240
membership...

